  "verdict": "Symanzik continuum extrapolation gives (alpha_xi, beta_pi, D_Omega) -> (0.105, 0.530, 0.785). The match D_Omega ~ pi/4 = 0.7854 is striking (0.05%) and the match alpha_xi ~ gamma_canonical = 0.10 is suggestive (5%). However the C2 constraint D_Omega = beta_pi - gamma is VIOLATED at continuum (diff +0.65), so the Symanzik triple is not a coherent framework solution. The right interpretation is either: (a) the canonical (9/10, 15/16, 67/80) is the N=50 anchor reading and Symanzik does not access the same algebraic system; (b) the per-regime calibration is inconsistent at different N and only N=50 is meaningful. Multi-N runs at N >= 1000 with alternative regime types would be needed to discriminate."
